<title>BANGLADESH: Bangladesh 1996/97 inflation below 4 pct.</title>
<headline>Bangladesh 1996/97 inflation below 4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>DHAKA 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bangladesh expects its inflation rate to be less than four percent during the 1996/97 fiscal year, ending June 30, Bangladesh Economic Survey released by the government on Thursday said.</p>
<p>The rate compares with 4.1 percent in 1995/96 and 5.2 percent in 1994/95 fiscal year.</p>
<p>The survey said the government's cautious monetary policy and controlled credit supply had hepled keep inflation under constant check.</p>
</text>
